-- expect: 99
-- Native tables, step 4: a table CROSSING A FUNCTION BOUNDARY, mutated by the
-- callee, with the mutation visible to the caller.
--
-- This is the SH-04 blocker in `src/selfhosting_matrix.zig`. Steps 1-3 in this
-- directory work because a positional table is register-exploded — one local per
-- element — which is fast and needs no memory, but leaves no contiguous storage
-- and therefore no pointer to hand across a call. A table parameter was DNB002,
-- a module-scope table DNB001, and a record with a table field DNB001.
--
-- `alloc_slots` gives a table a real frame region; a `ptr` parameter carries its
-- base address in x0..x7 like any integer-class argument; and `load_index` /
-- `store_index` with `ty == .i64` are scaled 8-byte accesses (`[base, idx, lsl #3]`).
-- Materialization happens at the first call that takes the table, and the name
-- is rebound to the base from that point on, so later reads see the callee's
-- writes instead of stale element registers.
--
-- The C backend cannot compile this, so it is gated on the declared answer.
bump(t: ptr): i64
    t[2] = 99
    0
end

at(t: ptr, i: i64): i64
    t[i]
end

main(): i64
    a = { 10, 20, 30 }
    z: i64 = bump(a)
    r: i64 = at(a, 2)
    r + z
end
